# Copy to `.env.deploy` and fill in. NOT used at Worker runtime — these are
# CLI-only credentials read by `wrangler` from process env when running
# deploys. Worker-runtime secrets (SMTP_*, MAIL_*, RECAPTCHA_SECRET) live in
# `.dev.vars` for local and `wrangler secret put` for prod.
#
# Where to get values:
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN  — https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
#                           Custom token with: Account → Workers Scripts: Edit,
#                           Account Settings: Read, Workers Routes: Edit (only
#                           if you set a custom domain route).
#                           Scope to a single account; set a 90-day TTL.
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID — `npx wrangler whoami` after `wrangler login`,
#                           or the dashboard sidebar.
#
# Load before running wrangler deploys (non-interactive):
#   set -a; source .env.deploy; set +a
#   npm run deploy:dev
#
# Or one-shot:
#   env $(grep -v '^#' .env.deploy | xargs) npm run deploy:dev
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=cfut_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
